@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nhi-il25-nouns`

-- National Health Insurance Law, s 2 ("income"), s 14(b), (c), (f1) and (g2): the income the
-- contribution is taken on, and the rates. Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from
-- line N of ../../registers/source-bundle/national-health-insurance-law-5754-1994.he.wiki.txt.
--
-- WHAT THE LAW DOES HERE. An insured person pays 5.17% of his income (s 14(b), (c)), and from the
-- contributions of January 2025 on, only 3.23% on the part of the income up to the reduced amount
-- (s 14(f1)); the employer pays for an employee and deducts it from his wage (s 14(b)(1)). "Income"
-- is the income from which the person is liable for National Insurance contributions (s 2).
--
-- WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY, AND WHAT THIS MODULE DOES ABOUT IT (NOTES.md, fork register):
--   F1  whether the maximum income of National Insurance Law Schedule K caps this income;
--   F2  whether that Law's s 348(b) raises a low income to Schedule K's minimum;
--   T1  what "the reduced amount determined under section 341" is (taken as the reduced collection
--       threshold of that Law's s 334(a); the text decides, it is not a switch);
--   T2  which payers (f1) reaches (the three it names; "neither" pays 5.17% on all of it).
-- The two forks are switches; the default declines where the two readings give different answers.
--
-- NOT HERE: the rate for months before January 2026 (the text printed 5% and the reduced rate was a
-- regulation, neither deposited), the National Insurance deduction (row IL-04), rounding (NOTES.md,
-- assumption A3).

§ `Sections 2, 14(b), (c), (f1) and (g2) — the income and the rates`

§§ `Section 14(b), (c): the full rate; section 14(f1): the reduced rate`

-- src:296 | (ב)(1) מעביד חייב לשלם למוסד דמי ביטוח בריאות בעד כל עובד מעובדיו שהוא מבוטח ושהמעביד חייב בתשלום דמי ביטוח לאומי בעדו, בשיעור של 5.17% [note: (עד ועד בכלל 2024, 5%; בינואר 2025, 5.16%)] מהכנסת העובד; המעביד ינכה את דמי ביטוח הבריאות משכרו של העובד.
-- src:298 | (ג)(1) מבוטח שהוא עובד עצמאי החייב בתשלום דמי ביטוח לאומי בעד עצמו, חייב לשלם למוסד דמי ביטוח בריאות בשיעור של 5.17% [note: (עד ועד בכלל 2024, 5%; בינואר 2025, 5.16%)] מהכנסתו.
@ref National Health Insurance Law s 14(b)(1), (b)(2), (c)(1), (c)(2) (source lines 296-299)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the full rate of section 14(b) and (c)` MEANS 5.17%

-- src:315 | (ו1) [note: (חל על דמי ביטוח בריאות הנגבים בעד חודש ינואר 2025 ואילך):] על אף האמור בסעיפים קטנים (ב) עד (ד) ו־(ה1), מעסיק החייב לשלם דמי ביטוח בריאות בעד עובד, עובד החייב בתשלום דמי ביטוח בריאות בעד עצמו ועובד עצמאי החייב בתשלום דמי ביטוח בריאות לפי אותם סעיפים קטנים, ישלמו על החלק מההכנסה שאינו עולה על הסכום המופחת שנקבע לפי סעיף 341 לחוק הביטוח הלאומי, דמי ביטוח בריאות בשיעור של 3.23%.
@ref National Health Insurance Law s 14(f1) (source line 315)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduced rate of section 14(f1)` MEANS 3.23%

§§ `Section 14(g2): income exempt from National Insurance contributions, counted in 2026 to 2035`

-- (g2) is a temporary provision "from 1.1.2026 to 31.12.2035". It adds to the income, for the
-- subsections (b) and (c), the income that s 350A(a) of the National Insurance Law exempts from
-- National Insurance contributions (a new immigrant's income on which he pays social insurance in
-- the country he came from). A month is in the period if its year is 2026 to 2035.
-- src:319 | (ז2) [note: (הוראת שעה מיום 1.1.2026 עד יום 31.12.2035):] בחישוב הכנסת מבוטח לעניין תשלום דמי ביטוח בריאות כאמור בסעיפים קטנים (ב) ו־(ג) תובא בחשבון גם הכנסה הפטורה מתשלום דמי ביטוח לאומי לפי סעיף 350א(א) לחוק הביטוח הלאומי.
@ref National Health Insurance Law s 14(g2) (source line 319)
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the month is within the temporary provision of section 14(g2)` y MEANS
    y AT LEAST 2026 AND y AT MOST 2035

-- "in subsections (b) and (c)": the four kinds those subsections reach. (e1) is not named, and (d)
-- is not, so the added income is not counted for them.
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of insured person under section 14`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 14(b) or (c) governs the kind` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an employee for whom the employer is liable for National Insurance contributions` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an employee who is liable for National Insurance contributions himself because the employer is not` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a self-employed person who is liable for National Insurance contributions himself` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an insured person who is neither an employee nor a self-employed person liable for National Insurance contributions himself` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `one who is paid an early pension, a retirement grant or an adjustment allowance` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an insured person for whom nothing is payable under section 14(b) to (e1) or (f1)` THEN FALSE

@ref National Health Insurance Law s 2 "income" (source line 52); s 14(g2) (source line 319)
GIVEN p IS A `A person's month under section 14`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income of the person in the month, with the exempt income section 14(g2) adds` p MEANS
    IF       `the month is within the temporary provision of section 14(g2)` (p's `year`)
         AND `section 14(b) or (c) governs the kind` (p's `kind`)
    THEN p's `income` PLUS p's `income exempt under section 350A(a) of the National Insurance Law`
    ELSE p's `income`

§§ `The income the contribution is taken on: the minimum (fork F2) and the maximum (fork F1)`

-- The Law is silent on both. s 2 defines income as the income from which the person is liable for
-- National Insurance contributions; that Law's s 348(a) disregards income above "the maximum
-- amount in Schedule K" for contributions under its s 335, and s 348(b) raises an income below the
-- minimum to it. s 15(b) of this Law applies the National Insurance Law's provisions, with the
-- necessary changes, to health contributions as if they were National Insurance contributions.
-- Whether that carries the maximum and the minimum over is not said. (The Institute's practice, and
-- the capstone's, is that the maximum applies; the text does not say so.)
-- src:52 | ”הכנסה“ – הכנסת עובד שממנה חייב מעבידו בתשלום דמי ביטוח לאומי, ולגבי מי שאינו עובד כאמור – ההכנסה שממנה הוא חייב בתשלום דמי ביטוח לאומי;
-- src:339 | (ב) ההוראות לפי חוק הביטוח הלאומי, לרבות ההוראות שנקבעו לפי פרק ט״ו סימן ה׳, יחולו בשינויים המחויבים לענין דמי ביטוח בריאות כאילו היו דמי ביטוח לאומי.
-- F2 first, then F1 (the maximum is never below the minimum, so the order does not matter to the
-- answer where both are readable).
@ref National Insurance Law s 348(b) (not encoded here); National Health Insurance Law s 2 "income" (source line 52), s 15(b) (source line 339); fork F2
GIVEN p IS A `A person's month under section 14`
      r IS A `A reading of the minimum income`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income after the minimum, for` p `reading the minimum income as` r MEANS
    LET gross MEANS `the income of the person in the month, with the exempt income section 14(g2) adds` p
    IN CONSIDER p's `minimum income for the person under Schedule K`
       WHEN NOTHING THEN gross
       WHEN JUST m THEN
           IF gross AT LEAST m
           THEN gross
           ELSE CONSIDER r
                WHEN `decline where the readings differ` THEN
                    REFUSE "section 14 does not say whether the minimum income of Schedule K raises an income below it, and the readings give different contributions"
                WHEN `the income is what the employee is paid` THEN gross
                WHEN `the income is raised to the minimum income of Schedule K item 1` THEN m

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(a) (not encoded here); National Health Insurance Law s 2 "income" (source line 52), s 15(b) (source line 339); fork F1
GIVEN x   IS A NUMBER
      f   IS A `The figures section 14 reads for a year`
      r   IS A `A reading of the income ceiling`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income after the maximum, for an income of` x `with` f `reading the ceiling as` r MEANS
    IF x AT MOST f's `the maximum monthly income`
    THEN x
    ELSE CONSIDER r
         WHEN `decline where the readings differ` THEN
             REFUSE "section 14 does not say whether the maximum income of Schedule K caps the income, and the readings give different contributions above it"
         WHEN `the maximum income of Schedule K item 1 caps the income` THEN f's `the maximum monthly income`
         WHEN `no maximum caps the income` THEN x

@ref National Health Insurance Law s 2 "income" (source line 52), s 14(g2) (source line 319), s 15(b) (source line 339); forks F1, F2
GIVEN p IS A `A person's month under section 14`
      f IS A `The figures section 14 reads for a year`
      r IS A `The readings section 14 is applied under`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income the contribution is taken on, for` p `with` f `under` r MEANS
    `the income after the maximum, for an income of`
        (`the income after the minimum, for` p `reading the minimum income as` (r's `minimum income`))
        `with` f `reading the ceiling as` (r's `income ceiling`)

§§ `The rates`

-- (f1): "the part of the income that does not exceed the reduced amount ... at 3.23%" for the three
-- payers it names (an employer for an employee, an employee liable for himself, a self-employed
-- person); the rest, and everything for any other payer, at 5.17%.
@ref National Health Insurance Law s 14(f1) (source line 315)
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      t IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tiered contribution on` x `with the reduced amount at` t MEANS
    `the reduced rate of section 14(f1)` TIMES (min x t)
    PLUS `the full rate of section 14(b) and (c)` TIMES (x MINUS min x t)

@ref National Health Insurance Law s 14(b), (c) (source lines 296-299)
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the flat contribution on` x MEANS
    `the full rate of section 14(b) and (c)` TIMES x

-- The payers (f1) names. (c)(2)'s payer, "an insured person who is neither an employee nor a
-- self-employed person liable for himself", is none of them, so (f1) does not reduce his rate:
-- T2. The Institute's page for those who are neither prints 5.17% on all of the income (its
-- worked example: 7,703 at 12.09% and 855 at 12.17%, each less 6.92% and 7% of National
-- Insurance being 5.17%); the text and the page agree.
@ref National Health Insurance Law s 14(f1) (source line 315); T2
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of insured person under section 14`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 14(f1) names the payer of the kind` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an employee for whom the employer is liable for National Insurance contributions` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an employee who is liable for National Insurance contributions himself because the employer is not` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a self-employed person who is liable for National Insurance contributions himself` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an insured person who is neither an employee nor a self-employed person liable for National Insurance contributions himself` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `one who is paid an early pension, a retirement grant or an adjustment allowance` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an insured person for whom nothing is payable under section 14(b) to (e1) or (f1)` THEN FALSE

@ref National Health Insurance Law s 14(b)(1) (source line 296)
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of insured person under section 14`
GIVETH A `Who is liable to pay the health insurance contribution`
`who is liable to pay the contribution of the kind` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an employee for whom the employer is liable for National Insurance contributions`
        THEN `the employer, who deducts it from the employee's wage`
    OTHERWISE `the insured person`

-- s 14(b), (c)(1) and (c)(2): the contribution on the income. For (c)(2) the amount is not less than
-- the minimum amount. For an income of nothing the rates give nothing; whether that leaves the
-- person within (f) is fork F5, applied by the module that chooses between the subsections.
@ref National Health Insurance Law s 14(b), (c), (f1) (source lines 296-299, 315)
GIVEN p IS A `A person's month under section 14`
      f IS A `The figures section 14 reads for a year`
      r IS A `The readings section 14 is applied under`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contribution under section 14(b) or (c) for` p `with` f `under` r MEANS
    LET x MEANS `the income the contribution is taken on, for` p `with` f `under` r
    IN LET rated MEANS
           IF   `section 14(f1) names the payer of the kind` (p's `kind`)
           THEN `the tiered contribution on` x `with the reduced amount at` (f's `the reduced amount`)
           ELSE `the flat contribution on` x
       IN IF   p's `kind` EQUALS `an insured person who is neither an employee nor a self-employed person liable for National Insurance contributions himself`
          THEN max rated (f's `the minimum amount`)
          ELSE rated
